    "kicker": "ARABIC101 / CHAPTER 07",
    "title": "Arabic numbers, made simple.",
    "subtitle": "A visual guide to recognizing, reading and writing Arabic (Arabic-Indic) numerals · Book pp. 127-132",
    "coreIdea": "Only the **shapes** are new. Arabic digits are written and read **left to right, biggest place first**, exactly like English: ٣٥ = **35**, ٢٠٢٥ = **2025**.",
    "coreIdeaNote": "Saying a combined number aloud: start with the biggest part and join the parts with وَ (and). With tens and units, say the unit first: ٢٦ = six and twenty.",
