            "title": "Bigger:",
            "text": "١٠٠٠ = أَلْف (ʔalf); thousands = آلَاف (ʔaa laaf); ١٠٠٠٠٠ = مِئَةُ أَلْف, the biggest number in the Quran. Also spelled مِائَة: the alif is **silent**."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Reading a long number",
        "bookPages": "127",
        "note": "Book pp. 127, 131",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "steps",
            "items": [
              {
                "title": "Read the digits",
                "text": "Left to right, like English: ٧٣٤٠ = 7340."
              },
              {
                "title": "Biggest part first",
                "text": "Thousands, then hundreds, then the rest."
              },
              {
                "title": "Join with وَ",
                "text": "Join distinct parts with وَ (and). With tens and units, say the unit first."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Look-alike digits",
        "bookPages": "128",
        "note": "Book pp. 128, 132",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "table",
            "compact": true,
            "columns": [
              "Digit",
              "How to tell it apart"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "٠ = 0 and ٥ = 5",
                "٠ is a small dot (not the decimal point '.'); ٥ is a round ring, not English 0."
              ],
              [
                "٢ = 2 vs ٣ = 3",
                "Count the bumps on top: one for ٢, two for ٣."
              ],
              [
                "٤ = 4 vs ٦ = 6",
                "٤ curls on the left; ٦ is a hook on a straight stem."
              ],
              [
                "٧ = 7 vs ٨ = 8",
                "٧ opens up like V; ٨ opens down like Λ."
              ]
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "exercisePages": "133-136",
    "exerciseTitle": "Use it on the exercises.",
    "exerciseIntro": "Drills plus six exercises: read, order, convert and spell. Exercises 2-3 need your own muṣḥaf.",
    "exerciseTips": [
      {
        "title": "Read left to right",
        "text": "The digit order is the same as in English: ١٥٧ = 157."
      },
      {
        "title": "Biggest part first",
        "text": "Thousands, hundreds, then unit + وَ + ten."
      },
      {
        "title": "Watch the look-alikes",
        "text": "٠ is a dot, ٥ is a ring; ٧ V vs ٨ Λ."
      }
    ],
    "exerciseGuide": [
      {
        "exercise": "Drills",
        "pages": "133-134",
        "task": "Trace each digit, then write and spell whole numbers",
        "method": "Follow the stroke arrows from p. 132. On p. 134, copy each number digit by digit from left to right, then write it in words: biggest part first, parts joined by وَ.",
        "example": {
          "ar": "١١٤",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "114 -> مِئَة وَأَرْبَعَةَ عَشَر"
        },
        "contrast": {
          "ar": "٢٣",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "23 -> ثَلاثَةَ وَعِشْرِين (unit first)"
        }
      },
      {
        "exercise": 1,
        "pages": "135",
        "task": "Put the aayaat numbers in ascending order",
        "method": "Convert each number to English digits first. Fewer digits = smaller number; with the same number of digits compare from the left.",
        "example": {
          "ar": "٩",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "9 comes first (one digit); key: 9, 10, 14 ... 157, 186, 279"
        },
        "contrast": {
          "ar": "٧٤",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "74, not 47: never read the digits right to left"
        }
      },
      {
        "exercise": "2-3",
        "pages": "135",
        "task": "Use your muṣḥaf: surah names for numbers, ayah totals for surahs",
        "method": "Ex 2: read the number, find it in the index, write the surah name. Ex 3: go to the surah and read the number of its last ayah.",
        "example": {
          "ar": "١٧",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "Ex 2 · 17 -> سُورَةُ الإسْرَاء"
        },
        "contrast": {
          "ar": "سُورَةُ الفَاتِحَة",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "Ex 3 · ٧ = 7 aayaat"
        }
      },
      {
        "exercise": 4,
        "pages": "136",
        "task": "Turn Arabic digits into English digits",
        "method": "Replace each digit one by one, keeping the same left-to-right order. Every ٠ dot is a zero; do not drop it.",
        "example": {
          "ar": "١٢٥٠",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "-> 1250"
        },
        "contrast": {
          "ar": "٥٠٥٠٠",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "-> 50500 · ring ٥ = 5, dot ٠ = 0"
        }
      },
      {
        "exercise": 5,
        "pages": "136",
        "task": "Match the numbers to their Arabic spelling",
        "method": "Find the biggest word first: آلَاف (thousands), مِئَة (hundred), a ten or a teen. Then the unit. Here the tens end in ـُون instead of ـِين: same number.",
        "example": {
          "ar": "أَرْبَعُمِئَةٌ وَأَرْبَعُون",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "440 · answer 5 -> b"
        },
        "contrast": {
          "ar": "أَرْبَعَةَ عَشَرَ",
          "translit": "",
          "note": "14, not 41 · answer 2 -> c"
        }
      },
      {
        "exercise": 6,
        "pages": "136",
        "task": "Spell out the Arabic digits in words",
        "method": "Split the number into thousands, hundreds and the rest. Write each part, biggest first, joined by وَ; for 21-99 write the unit before the ten.",
        "example": {
          "ar": "خَمْسَةُ آلَافٍ وَسِتَّةٌ وَسِتُّونَ",
          "translit": "kham sa tu ʔaa laa fin wa sit ta tun wa sit tuu na",
          "note": "5066"
        },
        "contrast": {
          "ar": "اِثْنَا عَشَرَ",
          "translit": "ʔith naa ʿa sha ra",
          "note": "12 · a teen, so no 'and'"
        }
      }
    ],
    "exerciseFooter": "**Two checks before you write an answer.** Did you read the digits left to right (٥٣ = 53, not 35)? And in words, did the unit come before the ten (ثَلاثَةَ وَخَمْسِين = three and fifty)?"
  },
